{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"custom","customType":"fugu-result","content":"```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Parse CLI options into a configuration dictionary and print it.\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\n\n\ndef build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        prog=\"cli.py\",\n        description=\"Parse CLI options into a configuration dictionary.\",\n        formatter_class=argparse.ArgumentDefaultsHelpFormatter,\n        epilog=\"Example: python cli.py --config settings.yaml --verbose\",\n    )\n\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--config\",\n        metavar=\"PATH\",\n        default=\"config.yaml\",\n        help=\"Path to the configuration file (not validated on disk).\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--verbose\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"Enable verbose output.\",\n    )\n\n    return parser\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    args = build_parser().parse_args()\n\n    # Convert the argparse Namespace into a plain dictionary.\n    config = vars(args)\n\n    print(config)\n\n    if config[\"verbose\"]:\n        print(f\"Verbose mode on. Using config file: {config['config']}\")\n\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n```\n\n### Usage\n\nSave as `cli.py`, then:\n\n```bash\n# Explicit arguments\npython cli.py --config settings.yaml --verbose\n\n# Defaults only\npython cli.py\n\n# Help text\npython cli.py --help\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n```text\n$ python cli.py --config settings.yaml --verbose\n{'config': 'settings.yaml', 'verbose': True}\nVerbose mode on. Using config file: settings.yaml\n\n$ python cli.py\n{'config': 'config.yaml', 'verbose': False}\n```\n\n```text\n$ python cli.py --help\nusage: cli.py [-h] [--config PATH] [--verbose]\n\nParse CLI options into a configuration dictionary.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help     show this help message and exit\n  --config PATH  Path to the configuration file (not validated on disk).\n                 (default: config.yaml)\n  --verbose      Enable verbose output. (default: False)\n\nExample: python cli.py --config settings.yaml --verbose\n```\n\nNotes:\n- `--config` defaults to `config.yaml`; the path is accepted as-is and never checked against the filesystem, so add an existence check if your workflow requires one.\n- `--verbose` is a boolean flag: present means `True`, absent means `False`.\n- To run it directly as `./cli.py`, make it executable first with `chmod +x cli.py`.","display":true,"timestamp":1785671237642}}
